# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env itself.
#
# Variables are grouped by module. A module should only read the variables
# under its own section — no module should reach into another module's
# config block. If a module needs a value another module also needs
# (e.g. an embedding provider key), that value belongs in the [shared]
# section, not duplicated per module.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [inference] — remote, OpenAI-compatible endpoints (shared)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All model inference runs on a SEPARATE machine behind an OpenAI-compatible
# API (ARCHITECTURE.md #10). This repo only sends requests to these URLs; it
# never downloads models or runs local inference. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
# Chat/completions LLM (used by intent_classification, query_rewriting, agentic)
# LLM_BASE_URL=            # e.g. http://<inference-host>:8000/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=             # token the endpoint expects ("EMPTY"/dummy if none)
# LLM_MODEL=               # served model id, e.g. Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
# LLM_TIMEOUT=60
# LLM_MAX_RETRIES=2
#
# NO per-request num_ctx here, by design: factory.py builds a plain langchain
# ChatOpenAI against LLM_BASE_URL's /v1, so this repo stays provider-agnostic
# and never talks to a server-native /api/chat endpoint. If the served model is
# also used by a consumer that forces a native context size, an unset value
# here falls back to the server's own default — when the two differ, the server
# reloads the model on every alternating call. Keep the fix outside this repo so
# the provider-agnostic boundary holds:
#   1. Per-consumer (preferred): the consumer builds its own BaseChatModel
#      that sets the context size and passes it to
#      retrieval.modules.intent_classification.LLMIntentClassifier instead of
#      this module's build_default_chat_model(). LLMIntentClassifier only
#      depends on langchain-core's BaseChatModel protocol, so this needs zero
#      changes here.
#   2. Machine-wide fallback: set OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH on the inference
#      server to the consumer's forced value, so context-unset /v1 calls
#      inherit it too. Blunter (it affects every model and caller on that
#      server); use only if a per-consumer fix is not an option.
# Thinking/reasoning suppression — OPT-IN. Only when explicitly set to `off`
# is LLM_THINKING_OFF_BODY (JSON, default {"reasoning_effort": "none"}) merged
# into every request; unset/on injects nothing (neutral). A hybrid-reasoning
# model left thinking on can spend the whole token budget on a hidden
# <think> block and return an empty/unparseable intent label — then set `off`.
# Unlike raw-HTTP clients, ChatOpenAI has no retry-without-body-on-rejection
# fallback, so a rejected body hard-fails classification; that is why
# suppression stays opt-in. Verify acceptance with the consumer's preflight.
# LLM_THINKING=off
# LLM_THINKING_OFF_BODY=
#
# Embeddings (used by top_n / raptor) — may be the same host or a different
# one; leave blank until that module is wired up.
# EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=
# EMBEDDING_API_KEY=
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=         # e.g. BAAI/bge-m3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [top_n]  (dense retrieval over an existing Qdrant collection)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The embedding model/provider is the shared [inference] EMBEDDING_* above (it
# must match whatever model wrote the vectors -- a mismatched model/size breaks
# search, see modules/top_n/README.md). This section is only the connection to
# the Qdrant instance those vectors already live in; this module never
# builds/writes the collection (the vectorization component does, on the GPU
# machine).
#
# QDRANT_URL / QDRANT_API_KEY / QDRANT_COLLECTION deliberately use the same
# prefix-less names the vectorization component uses for that instance, so one
# operator-facing naming scheme covers both sides. Consumers that live in other
# processes (e.g. the chatbot) read the same names from their own separate .env
# files -- no cross-process collision.
#
# QDRANT_URL=            # e.g. http://<gpu-host>:6333 -- fill in the
#                        # real address once vectors exist there
# QDRANT_API_KEY=
# QDRANT_COLLECTION=     # must match the collection name the vectorization
#                        # config writes to (e.g. medrag_chunks)

